<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tongmenghui</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a>–<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Chinese Revolutionary Alliance, Revolutionary Alliance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tongmenghui, or Revolutionary Alliance, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> founded in Tokyo in August 1905 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen">Sun Yat-sen</a> and other Chinese revolutionaries to overthrow the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>. It united several revolutionary groups and organised a series of uprisings in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution">Xinhai Revolution</a> it merged with smaller parties in 1912 to form the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tongmenghui.jpg" alt="Tongmenghui" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lu Haodong · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Naval_Jack_of_the_Republic_of_China.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
